        "problem": "Find the first three non-zero terms of the Maclaurin expansion of $\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1-5x).$\n\n$\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1-5x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$-\\,\\frac{625{x}^{4}}{4}+\u22ef$",
        "worked_solution": "The Maclaurin series for $\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1+x)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1+x)=x-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}+\u22ef.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReplacing $x$ with $-5x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1-5x) & =(-5x)-\\frac{1}{2}(-5x)^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}(-5x)^{3}-\\frac{1}{4}(-5x)^{4}+\u22ef \\\\  & =-5x-\\frac{25{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{125{x}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{625{x}^{4}}{4}+\u22ef.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
